   "is_new": true,
   "source": {
    "label": "thm:cucb individual",
    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "The $(\\alpha,\\beta)$-approximation regret of the CUCB algorithm in $n$ rounds using an $(\\alpha,\\beta)$-approximation oracle is at most \\sum_{i\\in [m], K_i>0} (\\ell_n(\\Delta^i_{\\min},p_i) \\Delta^i_{\\min} + \\int_{\\Delta^i_{\\min}}^{\\Delta^i_{\\max}} \\ell_n(x,p_i) dx ) + ((2+\\I\\{p^* < 1\\})\\pi^2/6 +1) m \\Delta_{\\max}"
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Regret is (alpha,beta)-approximation regret n*alpha*beta*opt - E[sum r_mu(S_t)], defined through expected rewards. Expression uses declared placeholder symbols for the sampling-threshold terms. In the classical MAB special case gives sum 6 ln n/Delta_i + (pi^2/3+1) m Delta_max (recorded separately)."
  },
